  {
   "approach": "Park at the Zopkios rest area off Highway 5 and walk east along the highway shoulder to a cairned climbers' trail that climbs steeply through forest and talus to the foot of Yak's big south-facing slabs. The climb starts left of Yak Crack, whose opening pitches follow a large dihedral that is easy to pick out from the base.",
   "area_id": "bc_yak_peak",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": null,
   "description": null,
   "discipline": "trad",
